<td id="S4.T5.3.1.9.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T5.3.1.9.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">58.4</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="S4.T5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation study of different resolution strategies within the MRA module.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Frames’ resolution allocation:</span> Table <a href="#S4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Q-Frame: Query-aware Frame Selection and Multi-Resolution Adaptation for Video-LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> analyzes how different numbers of frames with varying resolutions affect performance. To regulate the number of tokens, the quantity of frames for each resolution adheres to these guidelines:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K+\frac{M}{4}+\frac{N}{16}=8" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K+\frac{M}{4}+\frac{N}{16}=8</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The optimal configuration includes 4 high-resolution frames, 8 medium-resolution frames, and 32 low-resolution frames, achieving an accuracy of 58.4%. Further increasing the number of lower-resolution frames (up to 48) decreases accuracy to 57.4%, highlighting the diminishing returns of adding more low-resolution frames. Moreover, due to the necessary preprocessing in MLLMs, the number of tokens has increased slightly with the increase in number, which is generally acceptable. This suggests that the Q-Frame approach benefits from balancing the number of frames of different resolutions, optimizing computational load while preserving high accuracy.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S4.T6.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:496.9pt;height:146.1pt;vertical-align:-69.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(79.1pt,-23.3pt) scale(1.46721557454189,1.46721557454189) ;">
<table id="S4.T6.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T6.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" colspan="3">Frames</td>
